npm-debug.log
# Written from .npmrc.example, never committed.
#
# The stack's update-apps deletes .npmrc before it commits — correctly, since
# an .npmrc is environment config and in most apps it holds a token. Ours
# held no secret (the token comes from NODE_AUTH_TOKEN), but it was tracked,
# so `git add -A` would have staged its DELETION onto main. The next ship.sh
# builds from `git archive`, so the container would have had no registry
# config and npm ci would have failed with E401. Keeping it ignored and
# generated removes the conflict instead of arguing with it.
.npmrc
